*> Implementation test of the trim glue of ENTITY-ATLAS-BUILD (54 section 18.4 rule 4): a zombie in an iron helmet with a gold wild trim holds an atlas slot of the trim
*> texture (code 100518); with a pack that has textures/trims/entity/humanoid/wild.png (64 x 32: A0A0A0 at (0, 0), 606060 at (1, 0), a clear A0A0A0 at (2, 0), 123456 at
*> (3, 0)) the atlas rebuilt from the pack holds the texture recoloured with the gold palette: DEB12D, A0450A, the clear texel unchanged and 123456 unchanged.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ENTITY-TRIM-PACK.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CLMODELS.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(64) VALUE "build/client-test-trimkey".
 01 WS-DIR-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG VALUE 25.
 01 WS-NAMES               PIC X(256) VALUE "trimkey".
 01 WS-IDS                 PIC X(256) VALUE "file/trimkey".
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ROW-AREA            PIC X(66).
 01 WS-ITEM-ROW            PIC X(270).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG VALUE 10.5.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG VALUE 10.5.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ITEM                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SLOT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-B                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POS                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-JD                  PIC 9.
 01 WS-HEXDIGITS           PIC X(16) VALUE "0123456789ABCDEF".
 01 WS-EYE-TABLE.
    05 WS-EYE              FLOAT-LONG OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 01 B-ATLAS                PIC X(16777216) BASED.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-PACK-START" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIR WS-DIR-LENGTH WS-NAMES
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     MOVE 256 TO PL-HEIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO SK-U
     MOVE 10 TO WS-EYE(1) WS-EYE(3)
     MOVE 64 TO WS-EYE(2)
     CALL "ENTITIES-CLEAR" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "zombie" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ID
     CALL "MM-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW
     MOVE "iron_helmet" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ITEM WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-ITEM TO EN-EQ(1, 6)
     MOVE 5 TO EN-EQ-TRIM-MAT(1, 6)
     MOVE 18 TO EN-EQ-TRIM-PAT(1, 6)
     MOVE 0 TO EA-MT-COUNT
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SLOT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > EA-MT-COUNT
         IF EA-MT-TEX(WS-K) = 100518
             MOVE WS-K TO WS-SLOT
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "trim pack: the trimmed zombie holds an atlas slot for the trim texture 100518" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     IF WS-SLOT > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-PACK-ENABLE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-IDS
     SET ADDRESS OF B-ATLAS TO EA-ADDR
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-J
     PERFORM 4 TIMES
         MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
         MOVE WS-J TO WS-JD
         STRING "trim pack: atlas texel " WS-JD " of the trim slot" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
         COMPUTE WS-POS = ((EA-MT-Y(WS-SLOT)) * EA-W + EA-MT-X(WS-SLOT) + WS-J) * 4 + 1
         MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
         PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 3
             COMPUTE WS-B = FUNCTION ORD(B-ATLAS(WS-POS + WS-K:1)) - 1
             MOVE WS-HEXDIGITS(FUNCTION INTEGER(WS-B / 16) + 1:1) TO TL-OBSERVED(WS-K * 2 + 1:1)
             MOVE WS-HEXDIGITS(FUNCTION MOD(WS-B, 16) + 1:1) TO TL-OBSERVED(WS-K * 2 + 2:1)
         END-PERFORM
         EVALUATE WS-J
             WHEN 0 MOVE "DEB12DFF" TO TL-EXPECTED
             WHEN 1 MOVE "A0450AFF" TO TL-EXPECTED
             WHEN 2 MOVE "A0A0A000" TO TL-EXPECTED
             WHEN OTHER MOVE "123456FF" TO TL-EXPECTED
         END-EVALUATE
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
         ADD 1 TO WS-J
     END-PERFORM
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ENTITY-TRIM-PACK.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. MM-SPAWN.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, type (registry id), x y z (FLOAT-LONG), yaw (FLOAT-SHORT, also the head yaw): Add Entity.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-ADD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(16) VALUE LOW-VALUES.
 01 WS-V0                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V1                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V2                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-A0                  FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-X                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Y                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Z                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-YAW                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-TYPE L-X L-Y L-Z L-YAW.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER WS-UUID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-TYPE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-X
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Y
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER WS-V0 WS-V1 WS-V2
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-ADD
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM MM-SPAWN.

 COPY CLTEST.
 COPY PACKTEST.
